   "locked": false,
   "index": "b0121"
  },
  {
   "id": "jDP5o4EDKJJr553vEk6qu",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1514,
   "y": 677.5,
   "width": 436.8,
   "height": 245.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1689064611,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1553576200,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785777351988,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "index": "b0122",
   "text": "WHAT ONE STUDY CONTRIBUTES  (s_i)\n---------------------------------\n  meaningful benefit   +1.0\n  trivial benefit      +0.3\n  null / no effect     -0.3   <-- NOT zero\n  harm                 -1.0\n\nA well-run trial that found nothing is evidence\nAGAINST, not an absence of evidence. Competitors\ncount studies; counting studies rewards a supplement\nfor being tested and failing.\n\nException: for an ADVERSE-EVENT outcome a null is\nreassurance, and is scored as such.",
   "originalText": "WHAT ONE STUDY CONTRIBUTES  (s_i)\n---------------------------------\n  meaningful benefit   +1.0\n  trivial benefit      +0.3\n  null / no effect     -0.3   <-- NOT zero\n  harm                 -1.0\n\nA well-run trial that found nothing is evidence\nAGAINST, not an absence of evidence. Competitors\ncount studies; counting studies rewards a supplement\nfor being tested and failing.\n\nException: for an ADVERSE-EVENT outcome a null is\nreassurance, and is scored as such.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gG4oa9_9yRS2J58NbBmuF",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1500,
   "y": 966.5,
   "width": 560,
   "height": 220.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
   "backgroundColor": "#ebfbee",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "dashed",
